            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, justice Alito: Could you answer yes or no if you are changing your position?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan: Please explain how you will interpret and apply the statute going forward."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia: When you say \"privacy,\" do you mean the prescriber's concern that people will know he prescribed certain drugs?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts noted that there is another interest besides the State's concern about health\u2011care costs, namely the physicians' privacy interests."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice BREYER, justice Breyer: Does the Constitution forbid controlling advertising to prevent false and misleading practices?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice SOTOMAYOR, justice Sotomayor: With the Internet and computers, there is virtually no privacy for individuals."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 66,
              "start": 66
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts: Were there findings with respect to the statute as enacted?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
            "evidence_ids": [
